1
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:12,980
Brighten up the peace and try to step away.

2
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:28,680
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling out.

3
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:35,360
Holding hands with Mom as she walked,
looking back over her shoulder.

4
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:42,320
Hey, that strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:53,540
So I tried walking on the arcade street's tiles,
only on the black ones.

6
00:00:55,940 --> 00:01:01,840
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten.

7
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:09,140
Even the politicians with their self-important faces,
and the blue-haired aunties who are a thorn in your side.

8
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:14,720
Try turning at that corner over there.

9
00:01:15,740 --> 00:01:19,940
You can meet everyone, everyone.

10
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:27,860
Over there is Kameari,
well, surely there's Kameari.

11
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:33,040
Everyone, come on over to our town.

12
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:34,640
Thank you.

13
00:02:05,940 --> 00:02:08,560
The SF Space Alien's Counterattack

14
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:13,060
Hey, Ryotsu! What is the meaning of this?

15
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:15,020
Well, this is...

16
00:02:15,020 --> 00:02:17,680
Oh no, isn't that Ryo-chan?

17
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:19,700
This is undoubtedly our senior, isn't it?

18
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:22,260
I-I'm...

19
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:26,960
I've never been so embarrassed in my life.

20
00:02:27,860 --> 00:02:30,280
Hey, Buchun, this isn't me, you know.

21
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:34,680
Come on, they say everyone has three
look-alikes in this world, right?

22
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:37,060
This guy must be my lookalike.

23
00:02:37,060 --> 00:02:38,320
You idiot!

24
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:39,480
Look here!

25
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:42,940
Here's Ryo-san,
all cheerful from his horse race bets, and

26
00:02:42,940 --> 00:02:45,620
they've even carefully listed his name,
haven't they?

27
00:02:45,620 --> 00:02:50,400
No, surely there was someone with the same
name among those three lookalikes, right?

28
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:52,800
There's no way someone like that exists!

29
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:55,620
Ryotsu is the one and only
great fool in this world.

30
00:02:55,620 --> 00:02:58,153
There's only you.
There can't be anyone but you.

31
00:02:58,203 --> 00:02:59,680
You're the disgrace of the Japanese police.

32
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:02,460
The source of all evil, the enemy
of mankind, the spawn of the devil.

33
00:03:02,580 --> 00:03:05,299
Well, look.
Admit that the person in the photo is you.

34
00:03:05,349 --> 00:03:06,860
Now spill it. Admit it honestly.

35
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:08,340
Get it all off your chest
and you'll feel better.

36
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:10,740
That was absolutely not me...

37
00:03:10,740 --> 00:03:12,711
You stubborn fool.

38
00:03:12,761 --> 00:03:15,360
I told you, it's not me.

39
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:17,658
Though no confession was obtained,

40
00:03:17,708 --> 00:03:20,100
it's clear that you committed the crime.

41
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:24,200
Therefore, as punishment, you are ordered
to work tomorrow, giving up your day off.

42
00:03:25,620 --> 00:03:28,980
That's too cruel! Tomorrow is the Kameyari
Memorial Day we've been waiting for!

43
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:31,040
I have plenty of other plans tomorrow too...

44
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:31,320
I'm doing it!

45
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:38,280
Your trivial plans
don't even count as plans!

46
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:38,740
Mu-chan!

47
00:03:39,740 --> 00:03:40,380
Go on, go!

48
00:03:40,380 --> 00:03:40,540
Yes!

49
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:42,020
Mu-chan!

50
00:03:49,260 --> 00:03:52,140
This is the fuel obtainable on Earth.

51
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:55,620
Go outside the ship and procure this.

52
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:57,060
Understood.

53
00:03:58,040 --> 00:04:00,500
But we can't go like this, as we are.

54
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:02,000
We must change our appearance.

55
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,820
Copy the Earthlings.

56
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:07,520
Hey, Reiko.

57
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:10,600
Tomorrow, even if I'm not there,
things will work out, right?

58
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:13,600
I was supposed to be taking the day off anyway,
you know.

59
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:15,440
I don't mind, though.

60
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:18,440
Isn't it a bad idea to
defy the Chief's orders now?

61
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:21,420
If you make the Chief any
angrier than he already is,

62
00:04:22,140 --> 00:04:23,780
it might not stop at just coming in to work,
you know.

63
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:25,720
That's right, senior.

64
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:28,580
Besides,
there's the shopping street event tomorrow.

65
00:04:28,580 --> 00:04:31,400
We can never have too many hands, after all.

66
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:34,680
Taking pictures like this, you bastard!

67
00:04:35,620 --> 00:04:37,240
Besides, outside of working hours,

68
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:39,560
what I do and where I do it is my own business,
isn't it?

69
00:04:40,220 --> 00:04:41,280
Freedom is all well and good,

70
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:44,600
but I think it has to be within the
bounds of a police officer's position.

71
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:46,060
Before you're a police officer,

72
00:04:46,060 --> 00:04:48,620
you need the common sense of an adult.

73
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:50,400
Who do you two think you are, you bastard?

74
00:04:52,220 --> 00:04:55,900
This is my overjoyed expression of love for horses,
losing myself completely!

75
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:58,200
Why should I be ashamed in front of anyone?

76
00:04:58,200 --> 00:05:02,840
I'm proud of who I was that day,
I really am!

77
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:04,440
Hallelujah!

78
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:12,960
Remote stop!

79
00:05:15,420 --> 00:05:17,460
Stop it! Hurry up and stop the car!

80
00:05:17,460 --> 00:05:17,880
Yes.

81
00:05:22,180 --> 00:05:23,660
What's wrong, Chief?

82
00:05:23,660 --> 00:05:27,500
Did you change your mind and decide
to drop what you said earlier?

83
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:30,340
Ryotsu, are you at the police box right now?

84
00:05:30,340 --> 00:05:32,680
That's why I'm answering the radio like this,
isn't it?

85
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:34,480
Have you been there the whole time?

86
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:38,000
Yes, Kankichi Ryotsu has been
working diligently here the whole time.

87
00:05:38,380 --> 00:05:40,560
So, Chief, let me have tomorrow off.

88
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:44,800
Maybe you've built up some fatigue.

89
00:05:46,440 --> 00:05:47,960
Let's head home early today.

90
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:52,360
The Chief suddenly started talking nonsense too,
damn it.

91
00:05:54,420 --> 00:05:55,720
Ryo-san?

92
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:58,440
You're all here together.

93
00:05:58,440 --> 00:06:01,500
What are you talking about?
More importantly, have you already changed?

94
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:05,360
That earlier thing was about tomorrow's
night-shift assignment, right?

95
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:07,120
No, that was pretty good.

96
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:11,340
Anyway,
please take care of that matter tomorrow.

97
00:06:12,220 --> 00:06:14,020
Ryo-san,
you really do go all out, don't you?

98
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:16,080
What on earth was that?

99
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,160
Officer...

100
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:28,860
Why is he dead?

101
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:31,420
Where did you come from?

102
00:06:32,020 --> 00:06:33,280
Are you okay? Sorry.

103
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:34,240
Where's the car?

104
00:06:34,340 --> 00:06:34,660
Whoa!

105
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:37,860
W-what, seriously!

106
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:40,880
Aah! What was it again!

107
00:06:41,020 --> 00:06:42,780
No! I'm a police officer!

108
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:49,540
Akyaa, akyaa, akyaa!

109
00:06:51,060 --> 00:06:53,440
Wait, you! Why do you look exactly like me?

110
00:06:54,020 --> 00:06:57,300
And why are you so fast at running away!

111
00:07:01,660 --> 00:07:05,380
You bastard!
Explain why you look just like me! Hey!

112
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:06,960
Hey, hey!

113
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:07,820
Like I'd tell you!

114
00:07:08,120 --> 00:07:09,972
I found it in a trash can.

115
00:07:10,022 --> 00:07:12,400
So I copied it.

116
00:07:12,580 --> 00:07:13,040
Copied?

117
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:19,180
W-what the hell are you!

118
00:07:19,180 --> 00:07:24,520
Whoa! I'm an alien!
My UFO ran out of fuel, so I came to Earth!

119
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:28,520
I'm looking for this! Help me!

120
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:37,540
Is this the fuel for your UFO?

121
00:07:38,180 --> 00:07:42,920
Yes! Without it, we can't return to our planet!
Help us!

122
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:46,840
You can change your appearance at will?

123
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:47,920
Yes, that's right!

124
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:50,000
Anytime,

125
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:51,720
anywhere,

126
00:07:52,480 --> 00:07:53,480
on anyone!

127
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:55,320
Transform!

128
00:07:55,320 --> 00:07:56,660
That's amazing!

129
00:07:56,660 --> 00:07:57,940
Well, of course!

130
00:07:57,940 --> 00:08:00,820
We're aliens who can become any kind of weirdo,
you know.

131
00:08:00,820 --> 00:08:02,360
Don't use half-baked Japanese.

132
00:08:02,360 --> 00:08:03,620
I don't get it.

133
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:05,400
Practice Earth languages.

134
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:06,760
You practice!

135
00:08:07,220 --> 00:08:07,800
Listen up.

136
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:11,940
This fuel is a precious commodity
that's extremely hard to get on Earth.

137
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:12,880
Lucky!

138
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:14,220
So, be disappointed, I said.

139
00:08:14,220 --> 00:08:15,260
But, you know,

140
00:08:15,260 --> 00:08:17,900
if I cooperate, we might be able to get it.

141
00:08:17,900 --> 00:08:18,600
Really?

142
00:08:19,180 --> 00:08:21,900
In return,
you have to cooperate with me too.

143
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:25,340
Reiko, did you read the morning paper?

144
00:08:25,660 --> 00:08:26,540
What is it?

145
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:28,060
Look, here.

146
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:31,200
The article about the UFO crash.

147
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:35,100
Apparently there were quite a few
reports from witnesses yesterday,

148
00:08:35,500 --> 00:08:37,920
but in the end,
they couldn't find the actual thing.

149
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:39,980
Kei-chan,
do you believe in UFOs or anything?

150
00:08:40,540 --> 00:08:42,160
Don't you believe in them, Reiko-san?

151
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:46,560
Well, if aliens exist,
I'd like to meet one at least once.

152
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:49,720
Hey, Ryo-chan would know all about this kind of thing,
wouldn't he?

153
00:08:50,080 --> 00:08:51,780
Senpai believes in them, doesn't he?

154
00:08:58,980 --> 00:09:00,051
I wonder what's going on.

155
00:09:00,101 --> 00:09:03,340
Ryo-chan is acting like a totally different person today,
so serious.

156
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:07,520
I guess getting scolded by the
Chief yesterday really got to him.

157
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:09,680
But it's kind of creepy, isn't it?

158
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:12,100
I just hope he doesn't do
something bad out of anger.

159
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:19,200
Having a copy of yourself sure is handy

160
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:21,320
I'll keep that guy on
Earth for as long as I can,

161
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:23,460
and make the most of that copying ability.

162
00:09:23,460 --> 00:09:24,220
Ryo-san!

163
00:09:24,220 --> 00:09:26,740
Hey, Plamoya!

164
00:09:26,740 --> 00:09:28,380
What are you doing?

165
00:09:28,380 --> 00:09:29,660
Everyone's waiting for you.

166
00:09:29,660 --> 00:09:34,080
If we don't hurry,
Noriko-chan from Suekichi will show up!

167
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:36,180
What is this all about, anyway?

168
00:09:36,180 --> 00:09:37,460
What are you talking about?

169
00:09:37,460 --> 00:09:38,700
We promised yesterday, remember?

170
00:09:38,700 --> 00:09:39,260
Promise?

171
00:09:39,900 --> 00:09:41,140
So, Ryo-san...

172
00:09:41,140 --> 00:09:44,060
the stage for the Kameari
shopping street festival event

173
00:09:44,060 --> 00:09:45,900
It has to be set up by noon.

174
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:47,360
You'll help, right?

175
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:48,840
Yeah, yeah.

176
00:09:49,680 --> 00:09:50,840
That's not me!

177
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:54,260
We've checked thoroughly that
Ryo-san is off duty today.

178
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:55,860
Come on, hurry up, hurry up.

179
00:09:55,860 --> 00:09:57,400
So it's definitely not me.

180
00:10:01,580 --> 00:10:05,400
I have important business
and I have to head out now.

181
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:07,040
Important business, my foot.

182
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:09,240
It's probably a big horse race or pachinko.

183
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:10,540
Here, take this, will you?

184
00:10:11,180 --> 00:10:12,600
Please, Ryo-san.

185
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:15,240
It's the neighborhood association's big event,
you know.

186
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:18,720
You've got a backlog, haven't you, Ryo-san?

187
00:10:19,320 --> 00:10:20,483
All the lyrics you've been holding back on,

188
00:10:20,533 --> 00:10:23,720
you need to pay them all
back at a time like this.

189
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:26,440
Right, now that's settled,
shall we get you working right away?

190
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:34,260
We splurged to bring in a hot young idol,

191
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:37,700
so we'd better build a proper stage, or it'll
be a disgrace to the Kameari shopping street!

192
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:38,440
Whoa!

193
00:10:38,980 --> 00:10:42,420
Here it comes!
Wouldn't running have been easier than this?

194
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:47,080
Ryo-chan, why don't you take a little break?

195
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:50,280
That's right, senpai. You're not as young as you used to be,
you know, working since morning.

196
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:51,840
I'm fine, I'm fine.

197
00:10:53,220 --> 00:10:54,540
Switching posts.

198
00:10:55,360 --> 00:10:55,820
Nakagawa!

199
00:10:56,180 --> 00:10:56,500
Yes?

200
00:10:57,520 --> 00:10:59,760
Katsudon, ramen, and gyoza,
rush order, got it.

201
00:10:59,880 --> 00:11:01,820
You'll cover the bill for it.

202
00:11:04,880 --> 00:11:05,920
We're back to normal

203
00:11:08,020 --> 00:11:10,600
This is exactly the same as always,
isn't it?

204
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:21,540
Suekichi can't make it.

205
00:11:21,540 --> 00:11:22,500
He can't make it, you say?

206
00:11:22,500 --> 00:11:23,960
What do you mean by that?

207
00:11:25,340 --> 00:11:27,440
Suekichi's Noriko-chan can't come anymore.

208
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:30,980
Apparently, her morning drama shoot

209
00:11:30,980 --> 00:11:31,620
has said...

210
00:11:31,620 --> 00:11:33,220
Is that true?

211
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:37,420
She double-booked and got in a real bind,
apparently.

212
00:11:37,420 --> 00:11:40,400
And the drama's script is late,
so the production is at a standstill.

213
00:11:40,400 --> 00:11:42,440
So she cancelled at the
last minute or something.

214
00:11:43,060 --> 00:11:43,940
That's terrible, isn't it?

215
00:11:44,980 --> 00:11:49,400
The shopping street event itself was heavily promoted,
after all.

216
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:53,520
Crowds of fans will be pouring
in from other areas to see her.

217
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:55,700
If it goes badly, it could turn into a riot.

218
00:11:55,700 --> 00:11:59,520
I'm sorry, I truly apologize.

219
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:02,175
Sorry,

220
00:12:02,225 --> 00:12:04,480
Sorry.

221
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,480
This is bad.

222
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:18,100
What should we do?

223
00:12:18,100 --> 00:12:22,320
Could this actually be a
long-shot chance to make big money?

224
00:12:35,060 --> 00:12:41,220
Right, we had that. Let's do it. Without a crowd-pulling main attraction,
there's no point talking about it.

225
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:49,060
Well, the truth is, I've got a bit
of a connection with Noriko-chan.

226
00:12:50,060 --> 00:12:51,151
Here you go, Ryo-san.

227
00:12:51,201 --> 00:12:54,500
Could you add about 30%
on top of the original fee?

228
00:12:55,920 --> 00:12:57,260
30%!?

229
00:12:57,260 --> 00:12:58,260
Well, of course.

230
00:12:58,310 --> 00:13:01,462
Even with connections, we're practically
begging them to take the job, after all.

231
00:13:01,512 --> 00:13:05,100
There are all sorts of expenses involved, you know.
That's what the commission is for.

232
00:13:06,260 --> 00:13:08,600
Thirty percent is like a loan.
It'll pile up on you, you know.

233
00:13:09,640 --> 00:13:11,880
That betting tip from the other day paid out a huge upset,
you know.

234
00:13:12,260 --> 00:13:15,120
So what are you going to do? If you don't want to,
I don't have to buy it, but still.

235
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:15,980
About 100 yen.

236
00:13:15,980 --> 00:13:17,560
Then his eyes opened, this guy!

237
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:18,320
Here you go!

238
00:13:18,620 --> 00:13:20,420
So that's a yes, right?

239
00:13:20,520 --> 00:13:21,780
Nope, not OK!

240
00:13:22,880 --> 00:13:25,040
Listen,
this time you're going to become this guy.

241
00:13:25,180 --> 00:13:26,260
Take a good look.

242
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:28,460
Look closely!
You're the one who's supposed to look!

243
00:13:29,260 --> 00:13:32,480
Got it?
All of this is to get the UFO's fuel.

244
00:13:32,620 --> 00:13:33,300
Understand?

245
00:13:38,660 --> 00:13:39,740
W-why?

246
00:13:41,540 --> 00:13:43,220
Nozakanjaan!

247
00:14:05,340 --> 00:14:07,800
Great success, great success!

248
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:10,340
As expected of Ryo-san,
you really know everyone.

249
00:14:10,340 --> 00:14:12,500
You really saved us.

250
00:14:12,500 --> 00:14:13,980
Thanks, Ryo-san.

251
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:18,320
Then here's the promised

252
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:18,900
Is that so?

253
00:14:19,380 --> 00:14:20,540
Then I won't hold back.

254
00:14:20,540 --> 00:14:24,320
If you ever get into trouble again,
